    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns our top efficiency score of 82.13. His matchup against the left-handed Triston Rogers is mathematically favorable, amplified by an elite 18% park adjustment and a 4% bonus for a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher, which provides an ideal environment for him to exploit the league\u2019s scarcest category: stolen bases. Following him closely are **Christian Yelich** (70.78) and **Kyle Schwarber** (70.57); both benefit significantly from a favorable dynamic platoon split against Andre Pallante and Brady Singer, respectively. While **Trea Turner** remains a high-end anchor at 73.89, the lineup\u2019s overall efficiency hinges on the speed-oriented upside provided by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Lars Nootbaar**, who fell just short of the active roster with a score of 40.49. While he offers strong dynamic platoon upside against Logan Henderson, his projected low position in the batting order (-6% adjustment) and the opposing pitcher's respectable 3.03 xERA ultimately pushed him to the bench in favor of higher-floor plays like **Luke Raley** and **Carson Benge**. Managers should keep a close watch on **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth**, both of whom currently hold strong scores but carry a 33% rain risk. If the weather conditions deteriorate, their availability may shift, forcing a pivot to the bench. Despite their high xwOBA metrics, the bench remains deep today, as **Nelson Velazquez** and **Dillon Dingler** were excluded to prioritize lineup stability and matchup-specific platoon advantages.",
